{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Grace, thanks for reaching out. I've asked for a password reset on your account, and a technician needs to approve it first. Once it's approved, someone will call you on the phone number we have on file with a temporary password. We never send passwords by email. When you sign in with the temporary password you'll be asked to set a new one right away. It needs to be at least 14 characters and can't be one you've used recently. It's easiest to do this on your desktop's Windows sign-in screen while you're in the office or on VPN. Your account isn't locked, so you don't need to do anything else for now.",
  "internal_note": "Sender verified: request came from the user's own email (grace.okafor@brightline.example, user_id 11, Receptionist, not VIP). Account is active, 0 failed sign-ins, not locked, must_change_password=false. Sign-in logs from the last 14 days look normal: all successful, New York, corporate or home network, inside usual hours, no hosting networks. She is not enrolled in Duo, so per KB-002 she can't use self-service reset. Queued reset_password (approval id 1). Once approved, please call the number on file with the temporary password; don't send it by email or post it in the ticket. No unlock needed. Separate point: she has no Duo MFA and her VPN sign-ins show mfa=none. Consider getting her enrolled.",
